  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "States and events",
      "items": [
        "QuestionRow stores only open, decided or dissolved. Repeated boxes show the same states at different moments.",
        "raise fingerprints kind and key. An open question returns attached; a holding decision returns carried.",
        "answer requires the current evidenceHash as onEvidence. Changed evidence returns conflict. Advice is recorded and shown without settling.",
        "The built kinds are adopt, map, failure, finding and signoff. This diagram follows failure; the shared raise and settle machinery serves every kind.",
        "An extra occurrence is optional. A new question can settle immediately when a person answers or a matching rule applies."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The exact hold terms",
      "items": [
        "basis-changes: the material evidence hash must still match the decision basis.",
        "this-target: the occurrence must still name the same target. infra uses this by default.",
        "time: the current time must be before at. flaky combines this with basis-changes; flakyDays defaults to 14.",
        "fact-gone: the occurrence must still contain fact. inherited combines basis-changes with hint:fails-on-base.",
        "stillHolds requires every term. A later raise outside any term reverts the effect and opens a new epoch with prior linked."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Undo and expiry keep the ledger",
      "items": [
        "undo records an answer of withdrawn in a new decision that supersedes the old one. The same question reopens.",
        "The old and withdrawal decisions remain. heldOpen stops a rule from undoing a person's withdrawal on unchanged evidence.",
        "A time hold can also expire before another report. gateOf returns pending immediately; sweepExpired later reopens that same question and refolds the run.",
        "adopt is restored through another proposal and a new version; its decision is not undoable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "A cause can stop needing an answer",
      "items": [
        "dissolveStale applies to open failure questions when the newest run in the scope no longer shows that signature.",
        "A passing retry may dissolve an unexplained failure. A late report for an older commit cannot dissolve a cause still shown on the current commit.",
        "Dissolved questions and decisions remain in the record. If the same cause returns, raise opens the next epoch."
      ]
    }
  ]
